      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Jazz centres on swing feel, improvisation, and chord-progression literacy — grown from blues, ragtime, and brass band traditions."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lead-sheets",
      "title": "Lead sheets",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Melody + chord symbols; arrangement and soloing improvised. Standards (*Autumn Leaves*, *All the Things You Are*) shared like session tune titles."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "harmony",
      "title": "Harmony",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "ii–V–I, tritone substitutions, turnarounds everywhere. Rhythm section: walking bass, offbeat comping, ride cymbal swing."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "folk-crossover",
      "title": "Folk crossover",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Jazz voicings on song accompaniment; improvised choruses between tune repeats. Outline roots on strong beats first."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
